    "type": "numeric",
    "prompt": "Define the relation $A \\# B$ as $A \\# B = \\dfrac{A^2 - B^2 + AB}{2B}$. What is the value of $5 \\# 4$? Express your answer as a common fraction.",
    "image": null,
    "choices": null,
    "answer": "29/8",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Substitute",
        "body": "$5 \\# 4 = \\frac{25 - 16 + 20}{8} = \\frac{29}{8}$.\n\n**Answer: $\\frac{29}{8}$**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Split the fraction",
        "body": "$\\frac{A^2 - B^2 + AB}{2B} = \\frac{(A-B)(A+B)}{2B} + \\frac{A}{2} = \\frac{1 \\cdot 9}{8} + \\frac52 = \\frac98 + \\frac{20}{8} = \\frac{29}{8}$.\n\n**Answer: $\\frac{29}{8}$**"
      }
    ],
