    "type": "numeric",
    "prompt": "Define the relation $M \\,@\\, N$ as $M \\,@\\, N = M^2 + \\dfrac{2M}{N}$. Define the relation $A \\# B$ as $A \\# B = \\dfrac{A^2 - B^2 + AB}{2B}$. What is the value of $(4 \\,@\\, 2) \\# 10$?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": null,
    "answer": "25",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Inside first",
        "body": "$4 \\,@\\, 2 = 16 + \\frac{8}{2} = 20$. Then $20 \\# 10 = \\frac{400 - 100 + 200}{20} = \\frac{500}{20} = 25$.\n\n**Answer: 25**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Simplify the outer rule",
        "body": "$A \\# B = \\frac{A^2 - B^2}{2B} + \\frac{A}{2}$. With $A = 20$, $B = 10$: $\\frac{300}{20} + 10 = 15 + 10 = 25$.\n\n**Answer: 25**"
      }
